0,Mountain Koiali language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_Koiali_language,"Mountain Koiari (Koiali) is a language of Oro Province and Central Province, Papua New Guinea. It is not very similar to the other language which shares its name, Grass Koiari.","Koiali, Mountain",Trans-New Guinea
1,Music of Papua New Guinea - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Papua_New_Guinea,"The music of Papua New Guinea encompasses a wide range of traditional and contemporary styles developed across the country's highly diverse ethnic groups. Traditional celebrations known as sing-sing feature communal song and dance, and form a central part of cultural life.","Koiali, Mountain",Trans-New Guinea
2,Mountain Koiali language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/mountain_koiali_language,"Mountain Koiali is a Papuan language of the Trans-New Guinea phylum (ISO 639-3: kpx), spoken primarily by the Mountain Koiari people in the Central and Oro Provinces of Papua New Guinea, with an estimated 4,000 speakers as of the 2000 census. It belongs to the Koiarian family within the South-Eastern Trans-New Guinea branch and features a complex suffixing morphology, subject-object-verb ...","Koiali, Mountain",Trans-New Guinea
